<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb cocoa bean imports rise 64.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb cocoa bean imports rise 64.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in February totalled 5,539 tonnes, up by 64.5 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Feb 97	  Jan 97	 Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		5,539	   5,939	  3,367</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		4,276	   4,379	  2,408</p>
<p> Venezuela	     50	     247	    404</p>
<p> Ecuador		158	     229	    274</p>
<p> Brazil		 474	     590	    119</p>
<p> Malaysia	     175	     150	    151</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first two months of calendar 1997 were 11,478 tonnes against 7,805 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Feb 97	 Jan 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	   99		79	     233</p>
<p> Cocoa butter     1,708	   1,330	   1,213</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	 710	   1,001	   1,170</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p>  confectionery     871	   1,526	   1,115</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
